Everything passed on the first run, which is weak evidence, so I mutation-tested the suite: 27 deliberate divergences injected into [38;5;10mtranslation/src[0m one at a time. 24 were killed. One survivor was a genuine blind spot — commenting out [38;5;10mcounter = 0;[0m at the top of [38;5;10mcharinbuf[0m (lib.c:101) left all 35 original rows green, because modes 0/1/2/4/default never read the counter and mode 3 overwrites it immediately. It is only observable by seeding via [38;5;10mreset_counter[0m, calling a non-counter mode, then reading back through a low-level entry point. That became [38;5;10mCONFIGS.md[0m row 36 ([38;5;10mrow36_*[0m, [38;5;10mrow36b_*[0m), which now kills the mutant.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
